{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>הילכו</b> — He mentioned above: \"and concerning the prophets you commanded, saying, 'Do not prophesy.'\"" "<b>והנה אפקד עליכם</b> — \"I will make this known to you through My prophets; perhaps you will return to Me.\" Were it not that I made Myself known to the prophet and revealed My secret to him to reprove you, he would not prophesy of his own accord, for how could he know what I am about to do? And likewise His word does not come by chance. Now see: is it possible for two men to walk at one moment to one place for one purpose, if the one has not met with the other?! And when you see that the prophet's word was true, know that I sent him. And how can he defy the mouth that commands him not to prophesy, when you are the ones saying to them, \"Do not prophesy\"?!"], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:54.515042162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}